<title>USA: Earl Scheib Inc Q3 shr loss widens.</title>
<headline>Earl Scheib Inc Q3 shr loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>BEVERLY HILLS, Calif. 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Earl Scheib, Inc.</p>
<p>		  Condensed Consolidated Statements of Operations</p>
<p>		     For the quarter	   For the nine months</p>
<p>			ended Jan. 31,	     ended Jan. 31,</p>
<p>			 1997	   1996	  1997	  1996</p>
<p> Net sales   $ 7,869,000  $ 7,389,000 $35,799,000 $32,062,000</p>
<p>Operating income</p>
<p>  (loss)     (1,975,000)  (2,004,000)   (502,000)   (638,000)</p>
<p>Income (loss) before taxes</p>
<p>		 (1,680,000)  (1,554,000)     292,000   1,680,000</p>
<p>Income tax (benefit)</p>
<p>  expense	 (28,000)     (36,000)	29,000	79,000</p>
<p>Net income</p>
<p>  (loss)     (1,652,000)  (1,518,000)     263,000   1,601,000</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per</p>
<p>  share	   (36 cts)     (33 cts)	 6 cts	34 cts</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>  outstanding  4,576,000    4,568,000   4,691,000   4,568,000</p>
<p>NOTE: Prior-year results include gains on the sale of real estate of $2,193,000 (about $0.46 a share), compared with $665,000 (about $0.14 a share) for the current year.</p>
<p>Comparable-shop sales for the quarter and first nine months increased by 6.7 percent and 14.3 percent, compared with the same-quarter and nine-month periods last year, respectively.</p>
